The auth system is fixed and verified. There were **three distinct bugs**, and all three are now resolved in the code.

## What was broken

**1. Session cookie decoded with the wrong strategy** — [lib/auth/session.ts](lib/auth/session.ts)

The server config enables Better Auth's cookie cache without a `strategy`, so it encodes the `better-auth.session_data` cookie with better-auth's default **compact** strategy (base64url JSON + HMAC). But `getSession()` read it back with `strategy: "jwt"` passed to `getCookieCache`, so HMAC/verification always failed, the session read back as `null`, and everything bounced to `/sign-in` even when sign-in had genuinely worked and written a valid session to the database. Fix: read the cache without a strategy override so it matches the server.

**2. Every session died 5 minutes after sign-in** — [lib/auth/session.ts](lib/auth/session.ts)

`getSession()` *only* read the short-lived cookie-cache cookie (5-minute `maxAge`) and had no database fallback. Once the cache cookie expired, the session read as `null` even though the real session cookie is valid for 7 days — you'd be silently signed out five minutes in. I reproduced this exactly on the timer. Fix: after a cache miss (including expiry), fall back to `auth.api.getSession()`, which verifies the real cookie against the database.

**3. Wrong-role requests crashed with a runtime error** — [lib/auth/gate.tsx](lib/auth/gate.tsx) + the three dashboard layouts

The layouts passed a **render-prop function as children** to the async `RoleGate` server component. When the gate redirected an unauthorized role, that pattern crashed React's prerender pass: a student visiting `/admin/dashboard` got a "Functions are not valid as a child of Client Components" error page, and `/tutors/dashboard` hung empty. Fix: `RoleGate` now renders children as plain nodes, each layout moved its chrome into an inner async server component that re-reads the session (now memoized per-request with React's `cache()`, so no extra DB hit).

## Verified end-to-end

- Sign-up (student) → lands on `/students/dashboard` with the correct sidebar and account name
- Sign-in → dashboard renders; super-admin renders `/admin/dashboard` with the Staff menu
- Student visiting `/admin` or `/tutors` → cleanly redirected back to their own home (role isolation)
- Signed-out visitor → redirected to `/sign-in`; Logout → lands on the home page
- Simulated cache expiry (session cookie only, no cache cookie) → dashboard still renders via the database fallback
- `tsc --noEmit` passes; throwaway test account, debug scripts and diagnostics all removed — your two super-admin users are untouched

One caveat worth knowing: Turbopack kept a **stale bundle** of the buggy session module even after the edit until I forced a recompile, which briefly muddied the diagnosis. If your running dev server misbehaves again after a deep change, restart it rather than trusting HMR.

I also noticed the student dashboard itself hardcodes demo data ("Welcome back, Amaka") instead of the signed-in user's real courses — that's the known demo-data gap from my earlier walkthrough, not part of this fix.

